// Sample a 2D texture
//
// Read a colour out of a texture at a UV coordinate, with filtering and
// mip selection chosen by the sampler. Wire a `texture.texture_2d` node
// into `tex` and a `texture.sampler` node into `samp`.
//
// The texture and the sampler are separate inputs because WGSL keeps them
// separate: one texture can be read through a clamping sampler in one
// place and a repeating one in another, and one sampler serves every
// texture that wants its filtering. The mip level comes from the screen
// derivatives of `uv`, so this is a fragment-stage function.
fn sample_texture_2d(
    tex: texture_2d<f32>,
    samp: sampler,
    uv: vec2f, // @default 0.0, 0.0
) -> vec4f {
    return textureSample(tex, samp, uv);
}
